  "code": "2834",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9535%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RESULT IN U/mL&nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>REMARKS</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&lt;25</td>\n<td>Negative</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;25-30</td>\n<td>Grey zone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&gt;30</td>\n<td>Positive</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rheumatoid factor is an antibody directed against the Fc portion of IgG molecule. Polyreactive Rheumatoid factor (RF) is usually of the IgM class and is not specific for Rheumatoid arthritis. RF-IgM is also seen in chronic infections and other systemic inflammatory conditions. RFIgG &amp; RF-IgA have also been detected in Rheumatoid arthritis patients, of which RF-IgA has been associated with a more severe form of the&nbsp;disease with erosions and correlates well with clinical parameters and disease activity.</p>",
